// orient_exp_partial_migration.ri — CLI fixture pinning a KNOWN GAP in the
// #6080 loud-migration mechanism.
//
// `vec3(0, 0, 1.5708rad)` is a HALF-migrated rotation vector: the non-zero
// component was dimensioned, the two zeros were not. That mixes DIMENSIONLESS
// and ANGLE components, and `construct::eval_vec` collapses a mixed-dimension
// vec3 to `undef` at its OWN construction site — before `orient_exp` is ever
// called. The `E_RotationVectorDimension` classifier inspects `orient_exp`'s
// argument, so it never sees the offending vector and cannot fire.
//
// The observable result is therefore the OLD silent behaviour: `q = undef`, an
// `OpContractViolation` note, and exit 0 — no `E_RotationVectorDimension` line.
//
// This is deliberately pinned rather than left untested: it is the single most
// likely partial-migration typo, and it is the one case the loud-migration
// mechanism does not cover. Diagnosing a mixed-dimension container at its
// construction site is a separate, general concern (it belongs to `vec3`, not
// to the orientation family) and is out of #6080's scope. WHEN that lands, this
// test should be UPDATED to assert the new loud behaviour — not deleted.
//
// Lives in tests/fixtures/ (NOT examples/) to keep examples_smoke.rs green,
// since this file intentionally evaluates to `undef`.

module orient_exp_partial_migration

structure def OrientExpPartialMigration {
    let q = orient_exp(vec3(0, 0, 1.5708rad))
}
